  "description": "Shared Rust/WASM vector for root-holder enrollment authoring (#379, #381): device material validation, key fingerprints, and next_account_state refusals. Keys were generated with Node's own X25519/Ed25519, fingerprints computed with Node's SHA-256 over 'allw/device-key-fingerprint/v1' || 0x00 || kind || 0x00 || key (first 16 bytes, hex, groups of 4). Expected outcomes are written from docs/enrollment.md and the core module docs. Optional fields: 'repeat' (supply the states list that many times), 'account' ('other' expects the other root's account id), 'expect.replaced' (ids the change retires, #378). One sequence is u64::MAX, beyond JS number precision: read it as source text. States are signed at test time with the root seed [0x11; 32] (or [0x33; 32] for signed_by 'other'); device keys refer to the 'keys' table.",
